id: ops-gp0d
title: "A thirty-five second CLI test fails on timing whenever the machine is busy, so the gate reports red for load rather than for code"
description: "The test named installed pm CLI routes --repos values to every fleet command spawns the installed pm binary many times in sequence and takes roughly 30 to 35 seconds on an idle machine. On 2026-08-26 UTC it failed twice while six packages full gate suites ran in parallel, and passed when re-run alone on the same commit. It also passed on main under comparable parallel load. The conclusion is that the test is load sensitive rather than broken, so a red result from a parallel sweep must be re-run in isolation before it is believed."
type: Issue
status: open
priority: 3
tags[3]: ci,flake,test
created_at: "2026-08-26T20:06:09.002Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-27T14:01:20.140Z"
deadline: "2026-09-16T00:00:00.000Z"
author: claude
estimated_minutes: 90
acceptance_criteria: "The test either bounds its own runtime independently of machine load, or spawns the CLI once and asserts over the batch rather than once per command, so that a busy machine cannot turn it red"
repro_steps: Run the installed CLI routing test in test/ops.test.ts under concurrent host load. Packed pm package install can exceed its current 120-second subprocess timeout; fleet commands still use separate pm processes.
resolution: "Unresolved: the installed CLI routing test still spawns separate pm processes and remains load-sensitive. PR #101 improved packing but did not meet the batch-or-load-independent timing acceptance criterion. October 11 receipts record another packed-package-install timeout and failed full gates after a focused retry; timing acceptance remains unestablished."
actual_result: "Main 5804578 retains repeated spawnSync invocations. October 11 full gates remained failed after focused retry. A separate October 22 review again hit the unchanged packed-install timeout, then passed a focused retry and complete CI; recovery does not make the fixture load-independent."
comments[15]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-26T20:06:09.002Z",claude,Not introduced by the trusted-publishing change; that change touches only release.yml and its own test file.
  "2026-08-26T22:15:54.161Z",claude,"Corrected an internal inconsistency this record carried: the description claimed the commit passed in isolation on both re-runs while the note recorded a single isolated pass among three observations. Those cannot both be right and I cannot re-derive which from the surviving evidence, so both now state only what is defensible - two failures under six-way parallel load, and a pass when re-run alone on the same commit - without asserting a count of isolated re-runs that the records disagree about. Inconsistent evidence is worse than less evidence, because it misleads flake triage."
  "2026-09-07T21:04:03.704Z",codex-pm-ecosystem,"2026-09-07 UTC: reproduced the 30-second pm install timeout twice, including with a warm npm cache. The local-directory source copies development dependencies and generated files. Replaced that source with the actual npm-packed artifact and retained every installed CLI routing, SDK fallback, and package-doctor assertion plus both time limits. The packed test passes in 20.09 seconds (whole isolated file 56.48 seconds including setup). Reuses only the npm content cache; PM state and user configuration remain isolated. Full source gate pending."
  "2026-09-07T21:09:34.626Z",codex-pm-ecosystem,"2026-09-07 UTC: the complete release gate passed on installed published CLI/SDK 2026.9.7 and pm-changelog 2026.9.6. Final test summary {'tests': '464', 'pass': '462', 'fail': '0', 'skipped': '2'}; report All files                              |     100 |      100 |     100 |     100 |                   . Complete four-dimensional source coverage remains a separately checked scope, not inferred from a green label. Exact-head reviews remain incomplete where free bots are unavailable; no publication or private hosted-data deployment is authorized by this result."
  "2026-09-07T21:30:19.949Z",codex-pm-ecosystem,"2026-09-07 UTC CI follow-up: npm 10.9.8 runs prepare during npm pack despite --ignore-scripts and prepends prepare output to --json. The package step now removes inherited PM_PATH so prepare resolves its source checkout, and locates the single .tgz in the private pack destination instead of parsing mixed stdout. The actual installed-artifact regression passed with npm 10.9.8 (15.82 seconds test duration), and the complete local release:check passed again with unchanged 100/100/100/100 all-source thresholds. No installed-command timeout or assertion was weakened."
  "2026-09-07T21:32:48.014Z",codex-pm-ecosystem,"2026-09-07 UTC CodeRabbit review follow-up: the markdown receipt assertion previously matched Agent A anywhere, which could pass by matching the discarded column. It now requires a complete decision-row suffix with description / Agent B description / Agent A description in that order. The actual SDK merge-receipts markdown regression and typecheck pass. The structured receipt assertion already required B retained and A discarded; neither production semantics nor coverage thresholds changed."
  "2026-10-07T22:11:03.821Z",codex-sol,"Additional timing receipt from ops-3j1z: the first bun run release:check failed test/ops.test.ts installed pm CLI routes --repos values to every fleet command because packed pm package install hit its 30-second spawnSync timeout. The preceding npm full gate passed the same test and all 486 configured cases. Repair-specific tests and four coverage dimensions passed. An isolated installer retry and unchanged full Bun rerun are being used to distinguish transient execution delay from a package regression."
  "2026-10-07T22:14:34.119Z",codex-sol,"Isolated retry receipt: node --test --test-name-pattern=\"installed pm CLI routes --repos values to every fleet command\" test/ops.test.ts passed 1/1 with zero skips at the unchanged timeouts. The selected test took about 93 seconds; total including real merge-fixture setup was about 198 seconds. This supports a transient installer execution delay rather than a demonstrated pm-ops repair regression. Complete Bun release gate rerun is in progress with unchanged code and thresholds."
  "2026-10-07T22:20:16.262Z",codex-sol,"Final retry receipt from ops-3j1z: the unchanged complete bun run release:check passed 486 tests, zero failures, and 2 optional real-fleet skips; the packed --repos routing test passed in the full rerun. The initial timeout remains recorded as timing evidence. No timeout or threshold changed, and this owner item remains open."
  "2026-10-11T05:34:40.753Z",codex-agent,"PR #150 maintenance validation on the merged main/feature state: bun run release:check completed 597 tests, 594 passed, 1 failed, 2 existing optional fleet-data skips, 0 canceled/TODO. The sole failure was the existing installed pm CLI --repos acceptance: consumer npm install exceeded its unchanged 60-second child timeout with ETIMEDOUT. All measured coverage dimensions were 100 percent; lint, duplication and documentation gates passed. This enriches the existing timing owner instead of duplicating it. No timeout, threshold or test scope was weakened. An unchanged focused retry is pending after the required isolated-HOME full gate."
  "2026-10-11T05:35:15.549Z",codex-agent,"Correction to the preceding receipt: the consumer npm install had completed. The timed-out subprocess was pm package install of the packed artifact, invoked through runPm with the existing 30-second child timeout; the overall test elapsed about 60 seconds. Its assertion names ETIMEDOUT at test/ops.test.ts:714. The 597/594/1/2 suite counts and 100 percent coverage receipt are unchanged. No timeout was modified."
  "2026-10-11T05:52:40.542Z",codex-agent,"Unchanged focused retry passed: node --test --test-name-pattern=\"installed pm CLI routes --repos values to every fleet command\" test/ops.test.ts executed 1 test, 1 passed, 0 failed/skipped/canceled/TODO. The selected case took about 110 seconds; fixture setup made the total run about 292 seconds. The existing 120-second case timeout, 30-second pm package install child timeout and 60-second consumer install timeout were preserved. The full Bun and isolated-HOME npm gate receipts remain failed; this focused pass does not supersede their red status."
  "2026-10-22T12:22:43.388Z",codex-agent,"PR 188 review: fetched all three unresolved threads and every comment without pagination gaps; latest CodeRabbit review has no outside-diff findings. Merged main 5804578 before edits. Reuse this timing owner, correct its unsupported closure, correct both ops-pksh closeout fields, cancel duplicate ops-6ocs and regenerate CHANGELOG.md. Self-review also found stale ops-3xyb actual_result and generic ops-fcow inventory wording. Before-correction evidence against f48c86c fails 5/5 checks (0/5 passed, exit 1). Preserve all existing history records; no runtime or new closure changes."
  "2026-10-22T12:29:14.242Z",codex-agent,"PR 188 final evidence: original head f48c86c fails all 5 tracker-evidence groups (0/5 passed, exit 1); corrected records plus regenerated changelog pass 5/5. The same linked command passed through pm test --run --only-last --progress (1/1 linked command, exit 0). Rechecked all 22 reconciliation items against main 5804578 and retained implementation receipts; all referenced evidence paths exist. Whole-PR self-review additionally corrected ops-fcow inventory-only closeouts and ops-3xyb stale observed-result wording. Runtime, tests, workflows, manifests and committed dist are identical to main. All 23 changed history streams retain their complete main prefix. npm ci passed (163 packages added, 204 audited, zero vulnerabilities); npm run changelog:check and isolated pm health --strict-exit passed. No tracker-only full runtime gate is claimed. The pinned CLI needed JSON-quoted --add field values for the inline linked command; raw quoted/multiline input was parsed as extra metadata keys. No upstream issue was filed. Keep this load-sensitive timing owner open: successful focused/CI retries are not load-independent acceptance."
  "2026-10-27T14:01:20.129Z",codex-agent,"Related load-sensitive startup site observed during compatibility review: test/regular-input.test.ts gives the child 5 seconds including all static SDK and extension imports. A child executing only those imports exits successfully after 13.721 seconds on the shared host, before any artifact read is attempted. The unchanged test fails its external timeout in both full and focused runs. No timeout or assertions were relaxed; CI on a dedicated runner remains the full-gate evidence. This is a related bootstrap-budget limitation, separate from the original routing acceptance criterion."
notes[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-26T20:06:09.002Z",claude,"Observed three times on 2026-08-26: two failures under six-way parallel gate runs, one pass alone on the identical commit."
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-26T20:06:09.002Z",claude,"A red result from a parallel gate sweep needs re-running in isolation before it is believed, whenever any single test takes tens of seconds."
